1. **`view_bundle` is a direct path outside the 13 bound resolutions.** It accepts `as_of=None` and reads records directly; it is also used outside the two bundle entry points. Decide whether it resolves and validates its own bound or requires an already resolved one, then test direct calls as well as `/thesis-bundles`. A check for `default_as_of` calls alone will not catch an unchecked path. [Bundle](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/bundle.py:98).

2. **“The page is unaffected” is too strong.** A successful `/library` read supplies an eligible day. But if that read fails, the page silently keeps its embedded snapshot and later sends its day to `/ideas`. That day can be later than the service’s last completed day, producing the new refusal. Test both the successful live read and this fallback; document the latter behavior rather than claiming it cannot occur. [Page startup and Idea call](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/ui/src/bootstrap.js:193).

